  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: commons-io 2.11.0.rhlw-00009",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released commons-io:commons-io 2.11.0.rhlw-00009 with a backported security fix.\n\nCVE-2024-47554: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption vulnerability in Apache Commons IO.\n\nThe org.apache.commons.io.input.XmlStreamReader class may excessively consume CPU resources when processing maliciously crafted input.\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Commons IO: from 2.0 before 2.14.0.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 2.14.0 or later, which fixes the issue.\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for commons-io:commons-io 2.11.0 from Maven Central.",
